CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around current->thread.vm86->v86flags
#165: FILE: arch/x86/kernel/vm86_32.c:85:
+#define VFLAGS	(*(unsigned short *)&(current->thread.vm86->v86flags))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

ERROR:ASSIGN_IN_IF: do not use assignment in if condition
#225: FILE: arch/x86/kernel/vm86_32.c:251:
+		if (!(vm86 = kzalloc(sizeof(*vm86), GFP_KERNEL)))

Do not use assignments in if condition.
Example::

  if ((foo = bar(...)) < BAZ) {

should be written as::

  foo = bar(...);
  if (foo < BAZ) {

